<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel Corp rises on bonus issue news.</title>
<headline>Keppel Corp rises on bonus issue news.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in shipping to finance conglomerate Keppel Corp surged Singapore $0.20 to S$10.30 in the opening minutes of trade on Wednesday after the firm announced a one-for-four bonus issue on Tuesday evening, traders said.</p>
<p>The planned bonus issue was declared after Keppel announced a 4.7 percent drop in net profit to S$204.10 million for the year to December 31, 1996, in line with analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
